# Stable version family IDs, one per top-level vbare schema in engine/sdks/schemas/data.
# Format: `<id> <schema identifier>`. An ID is permanent: never reuse or renumber one, even
# after its schema is deleted, because heartbeats and persisted version marks carry it.
# The build fails when a schema has no ID or an ID names no schema.
# A protocol whose schema lives outside that directory is listed as
# `<id> <identifier> <min read> <max read>`; this binary writes its max read. Keep the range equal
# to the protocol crate's supported versions; a test in the crate that encodes it checks this.
# Such a protocol must be a message protocol that nothing persists: the storage incompatibility
# fence ignores it.
